 "result_text": "I fixed `parse_get_bucket_location` in `botocore/handlers.py`. I haven't run the issue's reproduction or any tests.\n\nThe handler already returned early when the response had a `LocationConstraint`. It now also returns early when the parsed response contains an `Error`. Previously a stubbed client error went on to read `http_response.content`, and a stubbed response has no raw body. That is where the `'NoneType' object has no attribute 'stream'` error came from.\n\nI assumed the stubber puts an `Error` key in the parsed response for `add_client_error`. I didn't confirm that. With the fix, `get_bucket_location` should raise the `ClientError` you specified, like `get_bucket_logging` does.",
